				<div class="grayBox mb20">
					<ul class="indent01">
						<li class="mb10">※A delay certificate certifies the maximum delay time incurred on that route and does not certify individual train delays. It also does not serve as proof of your boarding.</li>
						<li class="mb10">※For customers using the Shōnan-Shinjuku Line, please choose a certificate corresponding to the sections traveled on the Utsunomiya Line, Takasaki Line, Saikyō Line/Kawagoe Line, Yokosuka Line/Sōbu Line [Rapid], or Tōkaidō Line.</li>
						<li class="mb10">※For customers using the Ueno-Tōkyō Line, please choose a certificate corresponding to the sections traveled on the Utsunomiya Line, Takasaki Line, Tōkaidō Line, Jōban Line [Rapid], or Jōban Line.</li>
						<li class="mb10">※For customers using the direct-through trains on the Sōtetsu Line, please choose a certificate corresponding to the sections traveled on the Saikyō Line/Kawagoe Line or Yokosuka Line.</li>
						<li>※For customers using the Takasaki Line (Tōkyō to Ōmiya), please choose a certificate for the Utsunomiya Line.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<p class="indent01 font12">※Unauthorized reproduction, duplication, or modification of the information on this page in any electronic or printed medium is prohibited.</p>
			</section>
			<!--//路線別　遅延証明書-->
			
